    (2015, N'Chemistry', N'Organic Chemistry', N'Haloalkanes and Haloarenes', 92, N'Which of the following structural isomers of C4H9Br will undergo the fastest SN2 substitution reaction pathway?', N'1-Bromobutane', N'2-Bromobutane', N'tert-Butyl bromide', N'Isobutyl bromide', 'A', N'SN2 reactions are highly sensitive to steric hindrance. Primary alkyl halides (like 1-bromobutane) offer the most accessible path for nucleophilic attack compared to secondary or tertiary halides.'),
    (2015, N'Chemistry', N'Physical Chemistry', N'Chemical Kinetics', 93, N'For a first-order chemical process, if the rate constant (k) is 1.15 x 10^-3 s^-1, how much time is needed to reduce 5 grams of reactant down to 3 grams?', N'444 seconds', N'200 seconds', N'800 seconds', N'1000 seconds', 'C', N'Using the first-order rate formula: t = (2.303 / k) * log([A]0 / [A]t). t = (2.303 / 0.00115) * log(5/3) approx (2000) * (0.2218) = 443.6 seconds.'),
    (2015, N'Chemistry', N'Inorganic Chemistry', N'Coordination Compounds', 94, N'According to Valence Bond Theory, what is the geometric structure and hybridization state of the complex ion [Ni(CN)4]2-?', N'd2sp2, Square planar', N'sp3, Tetrahedral', N'dsp3, Trigonal bipyramidal', N'sp3d2, Octahedral', 'B', N'Cyanide (CN-) is a strong-field ligand that causes electronic pairing in the Ni(II) ion (d8), resulting in dsp2 hybridization and a square planar molecular geometry.'),
    (2015, N'Chemistry', N'Physical Chemistry', N'Chemical Equilibrium', 95, N'If the solubility product constant (Ksp) of Ag2CrO4 is 1.1 x 10^-12, what is the calculated solubility (S) of the salt in water?', N'6.5 x 10^-5 M', N'1.1 x 10^-4 M', N'3.2 x 10^-6 M', N'2.1 x 10^-5 M', 'A', N'For Ag2CrO4, Ksp = [Ag+]^2 * [CrO4^2-] = (2S)^2 * S = 4S^3. S^3 = Ksp / 4 = 1.1e-12 / 4 = 0.275e-12. S = cube root (2.75e-13) approx 6.5 x 10^-5 M.'),
    (2015, N'Chemistry', N'Organic Chemistry', N'Amines', 96, N'Which of the following reagents is specifically utilized in the Hofmann bromamide degradation reaction to convert an amide into a primary amine?', N'Br2 and KOH', N'Br2 and CH3OH', N'Br2 and H2O', N'Cl2 and NaOH', 'C', N'The Hofmann bromamide degradation involves the reaction of an amide with bromine and a strong base (KOH) to generate a primary amine containing one fewer carbon atom.'),
