    (2015, N'Chemistry', N'Organic Chemistry', N'Haloalkanes and Haloarenes', 117, N'Which of the following structural isomers of C4H9Br will undergo the fastest SN2 substitution reaction pathway?', N'1-Bromobutane', N'2-Bromobutane', N'tert-Butyl bromide', N'Isobutyl bromide', 'C', N'SN2 reactions are highly sensitive to steric hindrance. Primary alkyl halides (like 1-bromobutane) offer the most accessible path for nucleophilic attack compared to secondary or tertiary halides.'),
    (2015, N'Chemistry', N'Physical Chemistry', N'Chemical Kinetics', 118, N'For a first-order chemical process, if the rate constant (k) is 1.15 x 10^-3 s^-1, how much time is needed to reduce 5 grams of reactant down to 3 grams?', N'444 seconds', N'200 seconds', N'800 seconds', N'1000 seconds', 'B', N'Using the first-order rate formula: t = (2.303 / k) * log([A]0 / [A]t). t = (2.303 / 0.00115) * log(5/3) approx (2000) * (0.2218) = 443.6 seconds.'),
    (2015, N'Chemistry', N'Inorganic Chemistry', N'Coordination Compounds', 119, N'According to Valence Bond Theory, what is the geometric structure and hybridization state of the complex ion [Ni(CN)4]2-?', N'd2sp2, Square planar', N'sp3, Tetrahedral', N'dsp3, Trigonal bipyramidal', N'sp3d2, Octahedral', 'D', N'Cyanide (CN-) is a strong-field ligand that causes electronic pairing in the Ni(II) ion (d8), resulting in dsp2 hybridization and a square planar molecular geometry.'),
