    (2015, N'Physics', N'Mechanics', N'Gravitation', 137, N'If the angular velocity of the Earth increases such that the acceleration due to gravity (g) at the equator becomes zero, what is the length of a day in hours?', N'1.41 hours', N'24 hours', N'6 hours', N'12 hours', 'B', N'Effective gravity at equator g'' = g - omega^2 * R. Setting g'' to 0 implies omega = sqrt(g/R). Since omega = 2*pi / T, T = 2*pi * sqrt(R/g) approx 5060 seconds, which is ~1.41 hours.'),
    (2015, N'Physics', N'Modern Physics', N'Dual Nature of Radiation and Matter', 138, N'A photon and an electron have the same de Broglie wavelength. Which property is significantly larger for the photon?', N'Kinetic Energy', N'Linear Momentum', N'Velocity', N'Rest Mass', 'A', N'Both possess momentum p = h/lambda. For a photon, E = p*c. For an electron, E = p^2 / 2m. Given the comparable wavelengths, the photon''s relativistic energy is vastly higher.'),
    (2015, N'Physics', N'Mechanics', N'Units and Measurements', 139, N'If the velocity (v), time (t), and force (F) are chosen as the base structural units, what are the dimensions of mass?', N'F * v^-1 * t^1', N'F * v * t^-2', N'F * v^-2 * t', N'F * v^-1 * t', 'D', N'Dimensional relation: Force F = m * a = m * (v / t). Therefore, m = F * t / v = F * v^-1 * t^1.'),
    (2015, N'Physics', N'Optics', N'Wave Optics', 140, N'In Young''s double-slit experiment, the separation between the two slits is 3 mm, and the screen is placed 2 meters away. If the wavelength of the light is 600 nm, what is the fringe width?', N'0.4 mm', N'0.2 mm', N'0.6 mm', N'0.3 mm', 'C', N'Fringe width beta = lambda * D / d. beta = (600 x 10^-9 m * 2 m) / 3 x 10^-3 m = 400 x 10^-6 m = 0.4 mm.'),
    (2015, N'Physics', N'Electricity and Magnetism', N'Electrostatic Potential and Capacitance', 141, N'The electrostatic potential energy stored inside a capacitor holding charge Q and potential difference V is:', N'1/2 * Q * V', N'Q * V', N'1/4 * Q * V', N'2 * Q * V', 'A', N'Energy stored (U) is defined as the integral of work done charging, resulting in U = 1/2 * Q * V.'),
