    (2016, N'Chemistry', N'Inorganic Chemistry', N'Chemical Bonding and Molecular Structure', 114, N'Which of the following molecular species displays a perfectly linear spatial molecular geometry matching VSEPR layout rules?', N'XeF2', N'SF4', N'ClF3', N'H2O', 'D', N'XeF2 has 2 bond pairs and 3 lone pairs on the central Xenon atom. The lone pairs occupy equatorial positions in a trigonal bipyramidal arrangement, resulting in a linear molecular shape.'),
