    (2016, N'Physics', N'Electricity and Magnetism', N'Current Electricity', 137, N'A uniform copper conducting wire of initial electrical resistance R is stretched uniformly until its net length increases to exactly double its baseline measurement. Its updated resistance is:', N'4R', N'2R', N'R / 2', N'R / 4', 'C', N'Stretching a wire preserves its total volume (V = A * L). Doubling length (2L) forces cross-sectional area to decrease to A/2. Given R = rho * L / A, R'' = rho * (2L) / (A/2) = 4R.'),
    (2016, N'Physics', N'Modern Physics', N'Dual Nature of Radiation and Matter', 138, N'If the linear momentum of a free moving electron particle is doubled, how does its corresponding de Broglie wavelength scale?', N'It becomes halved', N'It becomes doubled', N'It increases fourfold', N'It remains completely unchanged', 'C', N'According to the de Broglie equation, wavelength lambda = h / p. Because wavelength is inversely proportional to momentum, doubling the momentum reduces the wavelength by exactly half.'),
    (2016, N'Physics', N'Mechanics', N'Gravitation', 139, N'The acceleration due to gravity (g) at a height h above the surface of the Earth equal to the planetary radius (h = R) scales relative to its surface value by what factor?', N'g / 4', N'g / 2', N'g / 9', N'2g', 'A', N'Gravitational acceleration varies with distance from the center via g'' = g * [R / (R+h)]^2. When h = R, g'' = g * [R / 2R]^2 = g / 4.'),
    (2016, N'Physics', N'Optics', N'Ray Optics and Optical Instruments', 140, N'A ray of light traveling from an optically dense glass matrix down into air encounters total internal reflection if its entry angle of incidence matches which criterion?', N'Greater than the critical angle', N'Less than the critical angle', N'Exactly 45 degrees', N'Exactly zero degrees', 'D', N'Total internal reflection takes place exclusively when a ray moves from a denser to a rarer medium and its angle of incidence exceeds the boundary''s specific critical angle threshold.'),
    (2016, N'Physics', N'Electricity and Magnetism', N'Semiconductor Electronics', 141, N'A structural p-n junction diode configured under forward bias parameters displays which electrical behavior across its boundaries?', N'Low resistance to current flow across a narrowed depletion region', N'High barrier resistance across an expanding depletion layer', N'Instantaneous structural breakdown under breakdown currents', N'Zero internal potential threshold values', 'C', N'Forward biasing opposes the internal built-in potential barrier, pushing majority carriers across the junction, which narrows the depletion layer and significantly lowers resistance to current flow.'),
